FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode wrote the file and still holds most of it. Douglas Christopher Wilson and alex94puchades are the next largest holders. Everyone else has a handful of lines.

I ran `surviving-lines --history lib/index.js` at HEAD. It uses `git blame -w -M -C` and covers all 238 lines.

**Who shaped it, oldest first**
- **Troy Goode** made the first commit on 2013-01-30. He has 29 commits, the last on 2026-04-10.
- **2013 to 2015:** about a dozen one-off contributors, such as Damien Klinnert, Simon Mansfield, Mathias Buus and Raymond Feng.
- **alex94puchades** made 5 commits in May 2015.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** made 4 commits between March and October 2017.
- **Later:** single commits from Benjamin Eidelman (2017), Tom Arad (2018) and LuisEGR (2021).
- In total, 23 people changed the file once the two Troy addresses are counted as one. Without that merge it is 24.

**Whose code is still in it**

| Person | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode (2 addresses) | 159 | 66.8% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9.2% |
| alex94puchades | 16 | 6.7% |
| Raymond Feng | 7 | 2.9% |
| max.laverse | 6 | 2.5% |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.5% |

- The remaining 16 people hold between 0 and 3 lines each. Damien Klinnert, Typicode, DracoBlue, jordandenison and Tomek Kopczuk have none left.
- Bus factor is 1, measured by lines: Troy alone holds 66.8% of the 238 surviving lines. Reaching 80% takes 3 authors. Both numbers are for this one file.

**Caveats**
- **Merged identities:** Troy appears as `<email redacted>` (147 lines, 28 commits) and `troy@laptop.example` (12 lines, 1 commit). The merge is a guess from names and addresses, and the tool rates the evidence as strong. I used `--merge-identities`, which works in memory only. I did not write a `.mailmap`. Unmerged, `<email redacted>` has 147 lines (61.8%), and bus factor is still 1.
- **alex94puchades:** the hint suggests this login is the same person as "Alejandro Caravaca Puchades" (same address). That is also a guess. In this file only the `alex94puchades` name has surviving lines.
- **Reformat commit set aside:** `62628c0`, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes" by Fiona Formatter on 2026-04-12. It changed only whitespace and quotes, so the table leaves it out.
  - Counted anyway, Fiona would hold 32 lines (13.4%), Troy 138 (58.0%) and Wilson 18 (7.6%).
  - Bus factor stays 1 either way.
- **Mechanical-rewrite check:** it examined 33 commits that hold surviving lines. It set aside only `62628c0`.
  - It flagged `fcd2b56`, Troy's "switch to ESLint; clean up" commit from 2015. I checked it with `git show --stat`. It touched 30 lines of `lib/index.js` along with the tests and config, and only 6 of its lines survive. I kept it, so those lines count as Troy's.
  - I did not re-run with `--ignore-rev fcd2b56`, so I have no figures without it.
- **Copy detection:** the figures use the default `-w -M -C`. The output printed no copy-detection note.
- **What the numbers can't show:** line counts say nothing about quality, review or design input. Code that was deleted counts for nobody.

